<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:55:48 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Residents leave Russian-occupied Oleshky in evacuation operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-residents-leave-russian-occupied-oleshky-in-evacuation-operation</link><description>
Residents evacuated from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have left for Russia's Anapa city with a Ukrainian delegation, senior official David Arakhamia said Friday. They are expected to fly to Belarus before returning to Ukraine by bus, during a rare ceasefire brokered by the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bebeee6e-d4a8-11f1-b250-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4WV4NU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bebeee6e-d4a8-11f1-b250-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4WV4NU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9a386dc-d4a7-11f1-91f9-57241323c8a7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:46:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bebeee6e-d4a8-11f1-b250-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4WV4NU.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Oleshky: No access to basic needs, ceasefire offers limited opportunity for humanitarian assistance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/oleshky-no-access-to-basic-needs-ceasefire-offers-limited-opportunity-for-humanitarian-assistance</link><description>
Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Jens Schumacher, Field Coordinator in Mykolaiv and Kherson with Solidarity International. Just a few kilometers separate the Ukrainian-controlled city of Kherson from Russian-occupied Oleshky. For civilians caught between military occupation, disrupted essential services and uncertain evacuation arrangements, geographical proximity offers little guarantee of access to life-saving assistance. Schumacher examines the humanitarian implications of a temporary ceasefire around Oleshky, where approximately 2,000 civilians were reported to remain. Although the cessation of attacks has created a limited opportunity for humanitarian operations, the geographical scope of the agreement, the prospects for evacuation and the possibility of sustained humanitarian access remain uncertain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6defaa90-d481-11f1-91a1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-143131-143934-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6defaa90-d481-11f1-91a1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-143131-143934-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73d178b2-d481-11f1-87b0-613a4a1fcb7d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:11:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'The International Criminal Court deserves the Sakharov Prize': CJEU President Koen Lenaerts</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261030-the-international-criminal-court-deserves-the-sakharov-prize-cjeu-president-koen-lenaerts</link><description>
We speak to the influential and long-serving president of the Court of Justice of the European Union (CJEU), Koen Lenaerts. The court is the EU's supreme judicial authority, responsible for ensuring that European law is interpreted and applied across all 27 member states.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95110bfc-d3a8-11f1-bee2-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-KOEN-LENAERTS.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95110bfc-d3a8-11f1-bee2-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-KOEN-LENAERTS.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a286a9e-d3ac-11f1-ae6d-8588e9e7894a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:51:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Star Wars: Has Russia's war with Ukraine gone intergalactic?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-star-wars-has-russias-war-with-ukraine-gone-intergalactic</link><description>
Russian made an unprecedented combative move this month as one of its military satellites, the Cosmos-2612, encroached upon the orbit of Ukrainian commercial satellite, Iceye-X36, in behaviour deemed "threatening" by the US State Department. Norbert Pouzin, an orbital analyst at French space tech firm, Aldoria, described the mercenary manoeuvre as the first of its kind.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d520738c-d15e-11f1-aecd-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/image1-183.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d520738c-d15e-11f1-aecd-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/image1-183.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d44473e4-d39f-11f1-a5a8-cbcd7a2d8799</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:29:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d520738c-d15e-11f1-aecd-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/image1-183.jpg">© KeepTrack.space</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Could US midterms impact the EU? Transatlantic ties hit new low after Trump-Putin diesel deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261030-could-us-midterms-impact-the-eu-transatlantic-ties-hit-new-low-after-trump-putin-diesel-deal</link><description>
From the EU's perspective, the second Trump presidency has felt even more destabilising than the first. From making the false claim that the EU was set up to "screw" the United States, to slapping tariffs on European goods, to making territorial claims on Greenland, to doing a diesel deal with Vladimir Putin and telling Ukraine to get a new president, Donald Trump has more than ruffled feathers on this side of the ocean. He has shaken the very foundations of the historical transatlantic relationship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c3484b0-d3ac-11f1-9ed9-399efcf9f4d0/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-DEBAT-EN-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c3484b0-d3ac-11f1-9ed9-399efcf9f4d0/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-DEBAT-EN-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77b0ebe0-d3ad-11f1-b0a0-612b886f0515</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:24:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French port strikes: Unions 'will get better working conditions', but can they curb militarisation?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-french-port-strikes-unions-will-get-better-working-conditions-but-can-they-curb-militarization-1</link><description>
Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Renaud Foucart, Senior Lecturer at the Department of Economics ECARES at Lancaster University. An international dockworkers’ strike brings into focus the relationship between organized labor, technological change and Europe’s expanding military investment. Foucart argues that port workers’ strategic position in global supply chains gives them exceptional leverage: “They know how powerful they are.” While questioning their ability to redirect military policy, he expects that leverage to secure concessions on automation and working conditions: “They can get those concessions. And I think they will get them.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f18d303e-d477-11f1-86d1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-131112-132013-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f18d303e-d477-11f1-86d1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-131112-132013-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6e49ff4-d477-11f1-82fa-3978b5243473</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:20:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>War in Ukraine: Evacuations under way in Russian-occupied Oleshky</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-war-in-ukraine-evacuations-under-way-in-russian-occupied-oleshky</link><description>
Starving and exhausted residents of Oleshky, a Russian-occupied town in southern Ukraine, were being evacuated on Friday, October 30, as part of a joint relief operation involving the opposing sides – the first operation of its kind in four years and eight months of war. FRANCE 24’s Ukraine correspondent Emmanuelle Chaze reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43c41370-d47a-11f1-9e50-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-456c9872.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43c41370-d47a-11f1-9e50-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-456c9872.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f408a76-d475-11f1-b7b8-293ded015169</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:01:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French crowd gathers for anti-islamophobia rally in Paris suburb after attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-french-crowd-gathers-for-anti-islamophobia-rally-in-paris-suburb-after-attack</link><description>
In France, thousands were protesting in the Paris suburb of La Verrière on Friday, a week after a racist terrorist attack killed one person and injured five others. The suspect, identified as Kevin T., admitted he was targeting people based on their appearance or religion and has been transferred to a Paris court. FRANCE 24's Morgan Ayre reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc7b2f58-d477-11f1-9fb6-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8202331a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc7b2f58-d477-11f1-9fb6-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8202331a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65818b22-d476-11f1-9fb4-b3f38f9aa0ea</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:51:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain working to identify train crash dead as relatives' anguish grows</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spain-working-to-identify-train-crash-dead-as-relatives-anguish-grows</link><description>
A second day of mourning is underway in Spain, with some families still waiting for news about missing loved ones, following Wednesday's high speed train crash that killed 69 people. Some have flooded social media with desperate appeals for information, posting photos or describing the clothes their relatives were wearing when they boarded the trains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4187d6b4-d470-11f1-a06c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26302685581510.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4187d6b4-d470-11f1-a06c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26302685581510.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9eecc20-d46d-11f1-82e7-adeef48f0c81</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:34:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Black Sea shipping under growing threats as drones hit container ships</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/black-sea-shipping-under-growing-threats-as-drones-hit-container-ships</link><description>
A Greek container ship has sunk after being struck by three drones, potentially of Russian origin, in the Black Sea off the Bulgarian coast on Wednesday, October 28. This incident highlights growing concerns for commercial shipping as the conflict between Ukraine and Russia persists.
 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cdb01a4-b353-11f1-b596-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8KZ4GJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cdb01a4-b353-11f1-b596-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8KZ4GJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7642c680-d46a-11f1-8213-1983d418e914</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:27:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spanish transport minister faces calls to quit after deadly train crash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spanish-transport-minister-faces-calls-to-quit-after-deadly-train-crash</link><description>
Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente faced calls to resign but ruled out stepping down on Friday. This follows Wednesday’s train crash in Toledo province, which killed 69 people. It is the country’s second high-speed rail disaster this year. FRANCE 24 correspondent Sarah Morris reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d06759c-d466-11f1-b9be-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c7b7c37f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d06759c-d466-11f1-b9be-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c7b7c37f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd9cac8c-d45c-11f1-9e93-e113a1b2af21</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:21:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Third weekend of protests looms as tensions persist across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-third-weekend-of-protests-looms-as-tensions-persist-across-france</link><description>
For the third Saturday in a row, people across France are set to take to the streets to protest against the high cost of living and demand better funding for education. Police are preparing for all eventualities ahead of another weekend of protests, following earlier demonstrations that ended in rioting and looting in city centres.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9a2506c-d45d-11f1-951a-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-130927-131111-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9a2506c-d45d-11f1-951a-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-130927-131111-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef086032-d45d-11f1-95c7-33050cbd318a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:10:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who is Kevin T., the main suspect behind the racist Trappes attack?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-kevin-t-the-main-suspect-behind-the-racist-trappes-attack</link><description>
France's anti-terrorism prosecutor on Thursday released details of the main suspect in the racist attack in Trappes and La Verriere, on the outskirts of Paris, on October 23.The 39-year-old opened fire with a submachine gun, killing 26-year-old Pengo Bossio Wangi and injuring five others.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeadaf9c-d467-11f1-8aab-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-30-at-14-23-41.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeadaf9c-d467-11f1-8aab-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-30-at-14-23-41.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6c1211c-d467-11f1-84fe-aba2da1ce04f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:06:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>Georgia's European dream left in limbo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261030-georgia-s-european-dream-left-in-limbo</link><description>
Two years ago in Georgia, tens of thousands of pro-European protesters rallied against the disputed results of the October 2024 parliamentary election, which was officially won by the ruling Georgian Dream party. A few weeks later, the authorities announced the suspension of the country's European Union accession process. Despite an ongoing crackdown, smaller-scale protests continue every day in the capital Tbilisi.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71d4e250-d3ba-11f1-ad40-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-EN-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71d4e250-d3ba-11f1-ad40-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-EN-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb199ede-d2eb-11f1-b617-d17d6f2c4016</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:34:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Maria GERTH-NICULESCU</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers</link><description>
While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d93e6f8a-d444-11f1-aaf8-15429d64cfb0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:06:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia's bastion of free press Novaya Gazeta shuts down under Kremlin pressure</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-russia-s-bastion-of-free-press-novaya-gazeta-shuts-down-after-years-of-kremlin-pressure</link><description>
Newspaper Novaya Gazeta, one of the last vestiges of independent journalism in Russia, announced Friday that it was closing down, citing pressure from authorities who recently searched the home of its senior editor and earlier this year detained one of its journalists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a425896c-d437-11f1-8330-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9PA86E-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a425896c-d437-11f1-8330-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9PA86E-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce7700a6-d437-11f1-99ac-779951003fb4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:42:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a425896c-d437-11f1-8330-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9PA86E-1.jpg">© Natalia Kolesnikova, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US approves potential sale of 500 Patriot missiles to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-live-russia-strikes-energy-facilities-kyiv-aid-convoy-heads-besieged-town-oleshky-ukraine</link><description>
The Trump administration has approved the sale of 500 Patriot missiles to Ukraine to bolster its air defences, the US State Department said Friday. Meanwhile, evacuees from Russian-occupied Oleshky have begun their journey back to Ukraine in a rare local ceasefire. Read our liveblog to see how the events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94fd74c6-d4ab-11f1-94d7-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4PF4MW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94fd74c6-d4ab-11f1-94d7-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4PF4MW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72ec2014-d431-11f1-aad6-6bfbde7fb7bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:28:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94fd74c6-d4ab-11f1-94d7-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4PF4MW.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>French presidential hopeful Édouard Philippe quizzed in embezzlement case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-french-presidential-hopeful-edouard-philippe-quizzed-in-embezzlement-case</link><description>
French investigators on Thursday questioned former prime minister Édouard Philippe, a candidate in next year's presidential election, in a case of alleged embezzlement of public funds. His lawyer welcomed the move, noting that magistrates had chosen not to place the ex-PM under formal investigation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d92c268-bc01-11f1-8bef-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/84109011edb91dfc4b0670eeca752d88a90ffe76.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d92c268-bc01-11f1-8bef-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/84109011edb91dfc4b0670eeca752d88a90ffe76.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b85f648-d429-11f1-b302-d7f75c420acf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:36:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d92c268-bc01-11f1-8bef-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/84109011edb91dfc4b0670eeca752d88a90ffe76.jpg">© Sébastien Salom-Gomis, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Canada and EU seek to 'withstand shocks together' through closer alliance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-canada-and-eu-seek-to-withstand-shocks-together-through-closer-alliance</link><description>
Canada and the European Union on Friday held talks to deepen cooperation on areas spanning critical minerals, artificial intelligence and trade; to better navigate global tensions and reduce reliance on the United States and China.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a1d0122-d423-11f1-9abe-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/458a2b32c7545f9fdfe1a142d1434ecd8bfaaef2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a1d0122-d423-11f1-9abe-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/458a2b32c7545f9fdfe1a142d1434ecd8bfaaef2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b2b578a-d423-11f1-86d4-fdcd08ea6b42</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:33:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a1d0122-d423-11f1-9abe-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/458a2b32c7545f9fdfe1a142d1434ecd8bfaaef2.jpg">© Christopher Katsarov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Let's reclaim our future': Thousands protest in Italy over rising living costs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-let-s-reclaim-our-future-thousands-protest-across-italy-over-rising-living-costs</link><description>
Thousands of protesters marched across Italy on Friday over the rising cost of living, education funding cuts and government spending on defence. Minor clashes were reported in the northwestern Italian city of Turin, while police maintained a heavy presence across the country.
